WEBVTT


c01
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.850
Legal says, freeze that PO.


c02
00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:04.830
It is already archived.


c03
00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:05.890
Now what?


c04
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:10.270
Follow one document through SAP ILM.


c05
00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:12.570
Business completion and residence checks


c06
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.090
determine whether it can be archived.


c07
00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:17.850
Live policies supply retention rules.


c08
00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:20.890
During archiving, IRM evaluates them


c09
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.850
and calculates retention dates.


c10
00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:25.750
The write program creates ADK files.


c11
00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:28.310
A separate store step transfers them


c12
00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:30.430
to ILM compliant storage.


c13
00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:33.170
The delete program removes archived records


c14
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.190
from the database.


c15
00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:37.070
Storage and deletion order is configurable.


c16
00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:39.810
A legal case identifies relevant objects.


c17
00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:42.010
Scheduled propagation applies holds


c18
00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:43.930
to existing archived data.


c19
00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:45.650
Held objects remain protected


c20
00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:47.410
even after expiration.


c21
00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:48.970
After minimum retention,


c22
00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:51.090
eligible data may be destroyed.


c23
00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.710
Maximum retention sets the destruction deadline.


c24
00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:55.150
Subject to hold.


c25
00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:57.290
Create the destruction work list.


c26
00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:59.830
Schedule the run and review the logs.

